NAME
       ssh-keyscan - collect the public host keys of ssh servers

SYNOPSIS
       ssh-keyscan [-t TYPE] HOST...

DESCRIPTION
       ssh-keyscan connects to each HOST and prints its public host keys in
       the format of ~/.ssh/known_hosts. Appending the output to that file
       lets ssh trust the hosts without asking the first time. Check the keys
       with the server's administrator if the network may not be safe.

OPTIONS
       -t TYPE
              Fetch only keys of this type: rsa, ecdsa or ed25519.

EXAMPLES
       Trust server2's keys for the current user:

           ssh-keyscan server2 >> ~/.ssh/known_hosts

SEE ALSO
       ssh(1), ssh-keygen(1)
